        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa-lab): unref detached qa cli child and detach stdio listeners",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`runQaCli` spawns a **detached** child (non-Windows) and attaches `stdout`/`stderr` `data` listeners that were never removed on `close`. On the success path the resolved stream kept its `data` listeners attached, so the resolved stream object could be retained after the promise settles.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis PR originally also added `child.unref()` to let a completed run not keep the caller alive. ClawSweeper review correctly noted (P2) that `child.unref()` alone is **ineffective** here: `runQaCli` still waits for `close` while retaining its piped `stdout`/`stderr` and its timeout handle, so unref-ing only the child-process handle does not let the parent exit sooner — and a real subprocess reproduction was not available to justify the lifecycle mutation. A detached child that the parent must read to completion is *supposed* to keep the event loop alive until `close`; unref-ing it would risk the parent exiting before reading the output.\n\nSo this revision **drops the ineffective `child.unref()`** (and the test that asserted it) and keeps only the legitimate, observable improvement: detaching both `stdout`/`stderr` `data` listeners in the `close` handler so the resolved stream is not retained.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- No behavior change to when `runQaCli` resolves (still waits for `close`).\n- Success path no longer retains `data` listeners on the resolved streams (cleaner teardown).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Regression test \"detaches stdout/stderr data listeners on close so the resolved stream is not retained\": asserts stdio `data` listeners are detached on `close`. Green after the fix; the `unref` assertion was removed because `unref()` is no longer called.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior or issue addressed: `runQaCli` in `extensions/qa-lab/src/suite-runtime-agent-process.ts` attached `stdout`/`stderr` `data` listeners that were never detached on `close`, so the resolved stream could be retained after the promise settled. The fix removes both listeners in the `close` handler. The originally proposed `child.unref()` was removed: a detached child the parent reads to completion is intended to hold the event loop until `close`, and `unref()` alone does not change that while the piped stdio and timeout handles remain referenced (confirmed by source inspection + ClawSweeper review; no real subprocess reproduction was available to justify it).\n\nReal environment tested: macOS 15, Node v24.18.0 (Homebrew node@24), vitest 4.1.9. The changed listener-detach path is driven through a mocked `node:child_process`.\n\nEvidence after fix (mocked child_process suite):\n- \"detaches stdout/stderr data listeners on close so the resolved stream is not retained\" -> listeners detached on `close`\n- \"runs the qa cli through the resolved node executable\" -> resolves with collected output\n\nObserved result after fix: the detached child is read to completion and both stream listeners are detached on `close`; the ineffective `unref()` mutation is removed so no unproven lifecycle claim remains.\n\nWhat was not tested: A real subprocess spawn against a live qa-cli binary was not executed (the spawn is fully mocked); the proof targets the exact changed lines — listener cleanup on `close`. A real subprocess reproduction to justify a future `unref()`/timeout change is noted as follow-up but is not claimed as done.\n\n---\n\n@clawsweeper re-review\n",
